- [N21] Node-level mutation: element=label(n5,c1,"After selecting preferred copy"); source=i2:After selecting a book, they can either view the book details or see a list of new copies. Alternatively, they can also view a list of used copies. -> i3:If they choose to view the book details, they have the option to then view a list of new copies or proceed to select a copy and end the process. -> i5:On the other hand, if they choose to view a list of used copies, they can evaluate the list and then select their preferred copy to complete the process.; reason=All four labels uniformly state 'After selecting preferred copy', imposing an identical precondition on edges that follow completely different steps (viewing lists versus selecting a generic copy). This alters the transition conditions and distorts the branching logic explicitly described in the source.
